<p>The backend directory retains the ArcticBase implementation name.
The product name is REFALL AB.
The bundled backend includes REFALL-specific APIs and state models.</p>
<h2>Work allocation</h2>
<p>A subject inventory supplies the denominator for coverage measurements.
Coverage units describe bounded work items.
Agents claim units before they submit observations.
Claim leases prevent indefinite ownership after an agent stops.</p>
<p>The standing loop dispatches work through the configured lanes.
Source research, binary review, runtime validation, and report preparation have separate roles.
Lane A uses Claude through ACP.
Lane B uses Codex through ACP.
Lane G is an optional worker that the host manager runs in a sandbox.</p>
<p>A subject-specific subloop can supply a harness, profile, device interface, or proof stage.
The core retains work allocation, evidence storage, and publication responsibilities.</p>
<h2>Persistent state</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Record</th>
<th>Purpose</th>
</tr>
</thead>
