<p>Workbench coverage uses <code>refall_coverage.db</code>.
The ledger uses <code>refall_ledger.jsonl</code>.
Subject runtime state uses <code>.refall/runtime/state.sqlite</code>.
Runtime artifacts use <code>.refall/runtime/artifacts/</code>.</p>
<p>The runtime database stores events, sessions, retries, artifacts, observations, and control signals.
The backend remains the authoritative store for workbench coverage, pending actions, capabilities, reports, and closeout state.</p>
<h2>Result processing</h2>
<ol>
<li>Receive a fenced <code>refall-submit</code> block from the specialist.</li>
<li>Validate the submission structure.</li>
<li>Store new findings and evidence.</li>
<li>Submit proposed finding transitions to the disposition gate.</li>
<li>Preserve unresolved work as pending actions.</li>
<li>Update coverage and the runtime manifest.</li>
</ol>
<p>The submission identity prevents duplicate application of the same result.
Source hashes identify evidence that depends on exact source or configuration bytes.
The disposition gate refuses receipts with stale source hashes.</p>
<h2>Gates</h2>
<p>The disposition gate requires evidence before a finding changes state.
The capability broker checks live actions against operator grants.
The closeout gate checks that research obligations and publication requirements are complete.
These gates preserve the reason for accepted and refused decisions.</p>
